<%# locals: (minor:, guardian: nil) %>
<%#
  Fuime Guardian Agreement, version 2026-09-11-v3.

  Changed from v2: §5 no longer describes a payment account opened in the
  guardian's name with Stripe. Production is merchant-of-record. Ninth Street
  Labs, LLC (the company that operates Fuime) is the seller of record; the
  guardian is the legal payee and clawback obligor, and must approve the payout
  destination before the first payout. What the app shows is a payable, not a
  parent-owned Stripe balance.

  This file IS the agreement text for that version. It is rendered both when a
  guardian signs and, afterwards, on the permanent record page — so a guardian
  can always re-read exactly what they agreed to.

  Do not edit this file to change the terms. Add a NEW versioned partial and
  bump Guardianship::CURRENT_AGREEMENT_VERSION instead: guardianships store the
  version they were signed under, and editing this text in place would silently
  rewrite what past guardians are recorded as having accepted.

  Note the version below is written as a literal, not as
  Guardianship::CURRENT_AGREEMENT_VERSION. v1 interpolated the constant, so the
  day the constant moved every historical v1 record would have relabelled itself
  as the new version while displaying the old text — the exact silent rewrite the
  paragraph above warns about, arriving through the version line instead of the
  terms.
%>

<div class="guardian-agreement">
  <p>
    This agreement is between
    <strong><%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %></strong>,
    doing business as Fuime (&ldquo;Fuime&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;), and you,
    the parent or legal guardian of
    <strong><%= minor.name.presence || minor.email %></strong> (&ldquo;the minor&rdquo;).
    By signing, you agree to the following.
  </p>

  <h4>1. You are the responsible adult</h4>
  <p>
    You confirm that you are at least 18 years old and that you are the parent
    or legal guardian of the minor. You accept legal responsibility for the
    minor's use of Fuime, including any business they operate through it.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are the person bound by this agreement. The minor is not, and cannot be
    — a contract signed by a minor is generally voidable, which is why the adult
    signs. Where Fuime's <%= link_to "Terms of Service", terms_path %> place an
    obligation on the account, that obligation is yours.
  </p>

  <h4>2. You consent to the minor's account</h4>
  <p>
    You give permission for the minor to hold a Fuime account and to operate a
    business through it. Without your active consent, the minor cannot create or
    run a business on Fuime.
  </p>

  <h4>3. You can see everything</h4>
  <p>
    You will have visibility into the minor's business activity on Fuime,
    including transactions, payables, and the people on their team. This is not
    optional and cannot be turned off by the minor.
  </p>

  <h4>4. You can withdraw consent at any time</h4>
  <p>
    You may revoke this guardianship whenever you choose, from your account or
    by contacting Fuime support. Revoking takes effect immediately: the minor
    will no longer be able to operate a business on Fuime. Amounts already owed
    to the business remain subject to the terms below.
  </p>

  <h4>5. Money and taxes</h4>
  <p>
    Fuime is a software platform, not a bank. Money moving through a business on
    Fuime may create tax obligations. Fuime provides records and summaries to
    help, but Fuime does not give tax or legal advice, and you are responsible
    for the minor's tax filings to the extent the law assigns them to you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %>, doing business as
    Fuime, is the seller of record on purchases. When a client pays, they buy
    from <%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %>. Fuime keeps its
    fee and owes the rest to the venture as a payable — not as a Stripe account
    you own, and not as a bank balance. You are the legal payee and clawback
    obligor. You must approve the payout destination before the first payout.
    Payouts go to that destination on a stated schedule.
  </p>

  <h4>6. What this agreement is not</h4>
  <p>
    Accepting this agreement records your consent. It is not identity
    verification, and Fuime does not currently verify that a person accepting a
    guardian invitation is the minor's actual parent or legal guardian. Do not
    accept this invitation on behalf of someone else.
  </p>

  <p class="muted text-sm">
    Agreement version 2026-09-11-v3, between you and
    <%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %>.
    Questions? Email <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %>.
  </p>
</div>
